<title>DUBAI: Emirates takes delivery of long-range Boeing 777.</title>
<headline>Emirates takes delivery of long-range Boeing 777.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-04-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dubai government-owned Emirates airline said on Sunday it had taken delivery of its first long-range B-market Boeing 777-200 aircraft.</p>
<p>The Rolls-Royce Trent-powered aircraft, which arrived in Dubai on Sunday, is the first of four B-market versions due to join the airline's fleet this year.</p>
<p>Three short-range A-market versions were delivered last year. Emirates has options for seven more.</p>
<p>The new aircraft has a range of 5,100 miles compared with the A-market version's 3,200 mile range, Emirates said.</p>
</text>
